<title>SOUTH AFRICA: DJI half yr shr up, mulls leisure move.</title>
<headline>DJI half yr shr up, mulls leisure move.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended Oct 31, 1996 vs 12 months to April 30, 1996</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Shr, (cts)</p>
<p>    - headline		14.1 profit vs 10.0 profit</p>
<p>    - attrib		  14.1 profit vs 173.4 loss</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   0.98 profit vs 12.07 loss</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   1.55 profit vs 11.68 loss</p>
<p>    Tax			 0.56	  vs 0.38</p>
<p>    Interest paid	   none	  vs 0.07</p>
<p>    Interest received     1.70	  vs 0.90</p>
<p>    Turnover		  0.15 loss   vs 0.26 profit</p>
<p>Full name: DJI Clothing Ltd. The company changed its name to Pacific Asia International Ltd on December 23, 1996.</p>
<p>NOTE - Directors said that during the interim period the firm, which changed its year end to June 30, remained a cash shell.</p>
<p>They said the company was now positioning itself to become a major player in the hotels, leisure, property and allied fields. Shareholders would be advised on any propsective investments.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
